# Layout alignment

No eyeballing. Vertical alignment is the parent’s job (`display: flex; align-items: center`), not per-child `margin` / `padding` / `top`.

## Shared row axis

Text, buttons, and icons in one row share one horizontal flex container that centers them on a single visual axis.

- Icons live in a **square fixed box** (e.g. 24×24) so the visual center does not drift.
- For icon + label rows, prefer `.icon-text` / `.icon-text-glyph` (`icon-text.mdc`).

## Two-line blocks (column isolation)

Icon/avatar on the side; title + subtitle are **one** vertical stack (`flex-direction: column`) beside it — not wrapping under the icon. Line 2 starts on the same left edge as line 1.

```
[ icon ]  Title
          Subtitle
```

## Anti-pattern

If you need a custom `margin-top` or a +2px height tweak to “line up” — the container grid is wrong. Rebuild the flex structure; do not nudge pixels.
